 For the current computational framework, this layer is implemented as a reduced pool-balance model with explicit MVB, ILV, docked-MVB, budding-precursor, and apoptotic-commitment states. Endosome maturation is represented as a Rab-conversion-supported source term for a secretory MVB pool, ILV loading is split into ESCRT-dependent and ceramide/tetraspanin-assisted branches, and MVB fate is biased between secretion and lysosomal loss by an acidification-sensitive routing term \cite{ott2025coordination,choezom2022nsmase2,villarroyaBeltri2016isgylation}. Small-EV release is then written as a Ca$^{2+}$- and SNARE-sensitive fusion flux from the docked MVB pool, while medium/large EV release is represented as a phosphatidylserine-, calpain-, and actomyosin-weighted budding/scission process. Apoptotic-body release is modeled separately as a damage- and blebbing-weighted branch so that injury-associated vesiculation is not conflated with productive secretory EV release \cite{liu2023snare,messenger2018munc13,pang2025arf,teixeira2020rock1}. This reduced formulation matches the current code implementation while preserving a direct path for later replacement with cell-type-specific Rab, SNARE, lipid, or apoptosis submodels as quantitative data become available.
 
